# 295 — بوابة علامات التعارض (حادثة أثناء دمج دفعات 37–39)
date: 2026-10-25  branch: m8/gate-conflict-markers  base: main 4972e9ca
category: governance gate (CI). No server code change. No production change.

## incident (my error, recorded as is)
After merging #251, rebasing m8/r171-s0-local-load onto main produced conflicts in the header lines of
ROADMAP.md / PROJECT_STATE.md and the top of CHANGELOG.md. My resolution script aborted on an assertion
(the HEAD side had 2 lines, not 1), but the same shell command went on to `git add` + `rebase --continue` +
`push --force-with-lease`. Commit 49b91804 was pushed to the PR branch with unresolved
`<<<<<<<` / `=======` / `>>>>>>>` blocks. The local gates run in that same command all PASSED:
no-delete, atomic batch v2, status evidence. Fixed by a separate commit 7ab87498 (entries 39, 38, 37 kept)
before CI finished; PR #250 merged only after CI on 7ab87498 passed. main was checked after each merge:
`git grep -E "^(<<<<<<< |>>>>>>> )" origin/main` ⇒ no hits (after #249, #251, #250).
Process lesson: never chain a conflict-resolution step with add/continue/push in one command.

## problem + acceptance (set before writing the gate)
problem: no gate detects conflict markers; a PR can merge them into governance docs or code.
acceptance:
- G1 the exact incident (3de45eac...49b91804) ⇒ exit 1 with each marker line listed by path:line.
- G2 the fixed tree (3de45eac...7ab87498) and current main (710997f9...origin/main) ⇒ exit 0.
- G3 only lines ADDED by the PR count; existing files with historical markers are not re-judged.
- G4 bare `=======` (common in recorded pytest output: 2 such lines exist in docs/audit/M6/logs/39_r072_after.log)
  is not a failure by itself; it is reported only alongside `<<<<<<<`/`>>>>>>>` in the same file.
- G5 non-ASCII (Arabic), quoted and space-containing paths are scanned, never skipped; CRLF handled.
- G6 git error (bad ref) ⇒ exit 2, never pass. G7 the governance workflow runs it.

## implementation
scripts/check_conflict_markers.py (stdlib; `git -c core.quotePath=false diff -U0 BASE...HEAD`; C-style path
unquoting; strips the TAB git appends after paths with spaces). Step "Conflict-marker check" added to
.github/workflows/governance-gate.yml (runs even if an earlier step failed).

## tests — tests/test_conflict_marker_gate.py (20)
two defects in my own first draft were found by these tests before commit (class: path handling):
- Arabic file name skipped silently (git quotes non-ASCII paths in `+++` headers) ⇒ fixed with quotePath=false + unquote.
- path with a space/quote char skipped (git appends TAB after such paths) ⇒ fixed.
red-first: test_workflow_runs_gate failed before the workflow step was added; the two path tests failed on the draft.

